.TH CODEX-USAGE-TRAY 1 "July 2026" "codex-usage-tray 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codex-usage-tray \- display OpenAI Codex usage limits in the Ubuntu system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codex-usage-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codex-usage-tray
starts an unofficial GTK 3 AppIndicator application that reads account state
and usage limits from the local OpenAI Codex app-server. It displays the
remaining allowance in the Ubuntu GNOME top panel.
.PP
OpenAI Codex must be installed separately. If Codex is signed out, the tray
displays a sign-in-required state and offers a Sign in to Codex... action that
starts the official Codex-managed ChatGPT browser flow. Users may also run
.B codex login
in a terminal.
.PP
When Codex is signed in, the menu can display the account email address and
plan reported by Codex. A successful browser sign-in is detected automatically,
after which account state and usage limits are refreshed immediately.
.SH MENU
.TP
.B Sign in to Codex...
Available when Codex reports that no account is signed in. Starts the
Codex-managed browser authentication flow.
.TP
.B Refresh
Checks account state and usage limits immediately. An automatic refresh also
runs every five minutes.
.TP
.B Quit
Stops the current tray process. The system autostart entry starts a new process
at the next desktop login while that entry remains enabled.
.SH DATA SOURCE AND PRIVACY
The application communicates with a local
.B codex app-server
subprocess to request account state and usage limits. It does not scrape
ChatGPT pages.
.PP
Codex Usage Tray does not directly read authentication tokens, browser cookies,
browser data, or Codex authentication files such as
.IR ~/.codex/auth.json .
Codex manages authentication and any network communication it requires. The
account email and plan returned by Codex are held in memory and displayed
locally; this application does not store or log them.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If the tray reports Usage unavailable, verify that Codex is available to the
desktop session with
.B codex --version
and authenticate with
.B codex login
if needed. Restart the application from the desktop launcher or run
.B codex-usage-tray
in a terminal.
.PP
Do not include credentials or authentication-file contents in bug reports.
Useful details are the package version, Ubuntu version, desktop environment,
and the displayed status message.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/codex-usage-tray.desktop
System-wide autostart entry used to launch the application after login.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.11 or newer, GTK 3, PyGObject, Ayatana AppIndicator, and a separately
installed and authenticated OpenAI Codex.
